<title>FRANCE: Usinor falls, Vallourec up on bid talk.</title>
<headline>Usinor falls, Vallourec up on bid talk.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in steel maker Usinor Sacilor fell, while those of Vallourec rose as rumours resurfaced on Friday of a takeover of the latter by Usinor, traders said.</p>
<p>Usinor officials were not immediately available for comment but a spokesman for tube-maker Vallourec denied the market talk. &quot;To our knowledge these rumours are without foundation and Vallourec is not for sale,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>Usinor was down 0.7 percent at 77.80 francs on turnover 520,095 shares, while Vallourec firmed 1.06 percent to 285 on 100,178 shares traded.</p>
</text>
